    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "This week is the anniversary of the songwriter, the birthday of the songwriter Jerome Kern. He was born January 27th, 1885. Kern wrote hundreds of standards like smoke gets in your eyes, all the things you are, the musical showboat, which included his favorite, Old Man River, as well as the Academy Award winning The Way You Look Tonight. Born into a nominal German Jewish family, Jerome Kern was not religious. One of his biographers wrote, his religion was his music and his lifestyle. Listen today for some of Kern's music, including Old Man River, the way you look tonight, and a fine romance.",
