    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95390.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "And yet the dawn is ours before we knew it. Somehow we do it. Somehow we've weathered and witnessed a nation that isn't broken, but simply unfinished. We, the successors of a country and a time where a skinny black girl descended from slaves and raised by a single mother can dream of becoming president. only to find herself reciting for one. When day comes, we step out of the shade of flame and unafraid the new dawn balloons as we free it, for there was always light if only we're brave enough to see it if only we're brave enough to be it.",
