    "turn_text": "Well, the threat was to the peaceful transition power, which is a part of our democracy. It's what our elections are about. It is, you know, in some ways viewed by the rest of the world as a miracle that every four or eight years we do this peacefully and often just really graciously. It's obviously not happened this time around because of Donald Trump and who he is. But it was just a dark and unprecedented assault on our democracy, literally. And yet it was also I think a wonderful day for the endurance of this work, which we didn't partake for granted. And if there is a silver lining in all this, I think maybe we'll take the institutions and this republic for Canada, a little less going forward.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_07",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "We will value the institutions and the republic less in the future.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The current moment has revealed the fragility of democratic institutions.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
